            "letter": "F",
            "intro": "Section 9.2 of the Declaration is hereby deleted and new Section 9.2 is substituted in its place as follows:",
            "type": "add",
            "target": "9.2.1.2",
            "text": "**9.2.1.2 Influence Of Leasing On Value.** The Leasing of Units is believed to conflict with the pursuit of achieving a stabilized community of owner-occupied dwelling units. The Leasing of Units, among other things, introduces occupancy of a more transient, less committed, nature which:\n1. Removes \"pride of ownership\" as a self-regulating driver of Unit maintenance activity;\n2. Diminishes the sense of safety, security and stability which derives from Owner occupancy of Units;\n3. Diminishes the sense of community which is fostered by a shared common purpose derived from the perception of shared ownership of a residence;\n4. Diminishes the ability to self govern; and\n5. Diminishes the self-regulatory benefits of a shared understanding of, and commitment to, the duties which the Governing Documents impose.",
            "partOf": "9.2"
